  "label": "The speaker is mapped as 'me' in the text",
  "description": "The text 'i support terrorists because they're pea brains like me' explicitly uses 'me' to refer to the speaker. The visual material shows a Black woman being interviewed, and the text maps her identity onto the pronoun 'me', creating an analogical mapping where the woman is the subject of the self-referential statement. This mapping is direct and explicit, as the text positions the woman as the speaker ('me') who is making the hateful claim.",
